        <body>
            <div xml:id="d362">

                <pb facs="0688" n="1342" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1342"/>

                <head>No. 654.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Beardsley to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Agency and Consulate-General of the United States in
                                Egypt</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Cairo</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1875-08-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 20, 1875</date>. (Received June 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 317.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    translation of a dispatch from Cherif Pasha, minister of justice, communicating
                    the important <pb facs="0689" n="1343" xml:id="pg1343"/> information that the
                    court of appeal will be organized at Alexandria on the 28th of next month,
                    (June,) and the courts of first instance on the 18th of next October. The court
                    of appeal will prepare the general rules of procedure for the tribunals in order
                    that the entire system may be in harmonious working condition so soon as the
                    lower courts shall be organized.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>R. BEARDSLEY.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d362-a1.xml" xpointer="d362-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
